A||||12||L.I. Fieros||Rode in a 911 today......some thoughts||||5||
Z||000000||L.I. Fieros||12-28-2001||01:11 AM||||My friend recently purchased a 1988 Porsche 911 (non-turbo 3.2 liter 6 cyl., 5spd).  It's the limited edition model.  The car is beautiful.  It only has 43K miles on it and has always been garaged so it's perfect.  Anyway, as we were driving along he began to tell me the stats on the car.  It's factory rated at 217hp. which comes out to be about 198hp. at the flywheel with all the accessories on the motor.  And it weighs in at 2700-2800lbs.  Well, after he got on it a little bit (it sings above 3500rpm.) I couldn't help but think that it felt exactly like my other friends 88GT Turbo 2.8 V6.  Except that the Fiero probably rides a tad bit softer and has a tad more power below 3000 rpm.  So, I got to thinking about the Turbo Fiero stats....220hp. and weighs 2800-2900lbs.  Now that's pretty close to me.  MAN!, why didn't Pontiac do this???  It would have been an incredible rivalry.  The feel inside the 88 Porsche is very similar to the 88GT Turbo.  DAMN GM!!!  One mid-engine, one rear-engine, manual steering, 200hp., 2 seaters (useable anyway), sloping front hood,.... I think it would have been awesome to watch the progression of the Fiero into the 21st century.  They could have taken on Porsche, for less than $20K!But alas we shall never know. Oh well.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>Later,<BR>Dave||||reg||5
Z||000001||JayLT1||12-28-2001||01:14 AM||||i have to agree, what the hell was gm thinking, The fiero could have beat the vette in nearly every aspect if they wanted to. A v-6 turbo would of been close to the TPI vettes and a v-8 whould have blown them away. and as for handleing i think the right suspention on a fiero could outhandle a brand new vette. my 2 cents<BR>j<P>------------------<BR>86 Black GT (95LT1 on the way)||||reg||1
Z||000002||frontal lobe||12-28-2001||02:10 AM||||You just answered your own question...the corvette.  I don't believe GM will EVER let one of their other performance models rival the corvette.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Posthumane||12-28-2001||02:12 AM||||That's exactly the point Jay. If the fiero outperforms the vette, then they would be selling a less expensive car to the people that may have otherwise bought the more pricey vette. It's all about money to them. sigh.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||1
