Z||000005||LoW_KeY||12-28-2001||05:12 AM||||That's why I think the bird and camaro were killed.. I know one of the firebirds had some nasty times.. 0-60 5.1 top end 163 governed bet ya chevy didn't like that one.||||reg||1
Z||000006||rogergarrison||12-28-2001||07:31 AM||||the 930 Porsche has an even longer nose and huge fender bulges. Have you seen the new 911 GT2. twin turbo, 0-60 in 3.8, 190+ top off the showroom floor. And if you see a pic of one, it looks like it has a Fiero rear wing, no 'whale tail'.||||reg||1
Z||000007||gtsonly||12-28-2001||09:08 AM||||I think it is like comparing apples and oranges. All those cars have different characteristics. Just because the cars have similiar HP rating does not mean they would perform the same. Just my thoughts!!!<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/myfiero001_copy_1.jpg"> ||||reg||7
Z||000008||artherd||12-29-2001||01:25 AM||||The Fiero (88s in good/slightly-moded condition at least) reminds me dynamically a LOT of the era's 911, and of the 308 Ferraris.<P>NOT bad company for our little cars!<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>PS: (Yes, I've driven both, and am talking about the overall 'feel' of the cars.  If you don't think a car has a 'feel' then I pitty your soul  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by L.I. Fieros:<BR><B>My friend recently purchased a 1988 Porsche 911 (non-turbo 3.2 liter 6 cyl., 5spd).  It's the limited edition model.  The car is beautiful.  It only has 43K miles on it and has always been garaged so it's perfect.  Anyway, as we were driving along he began to tell me the stats on the car.  It's factory rated at 217hp. which comes out to be about 198hp. at the flywheel with all the accessories on the motor.  And it weighs in at 2700-2800lbs.  Well, after he got on it a little bit (it sings above 3500rpm.) I couldn't help but think that it felt exactly like my other friends 88GT Turbo 2.8 V6.  Except that the Fiero probably rides a tad bit softer and has a tad more power below 3000 rpm.  So, I got to thinking about the Turbo Fiero stats....220hp. and weighs 2800-2900lbs.  Now that's pretty close to me.  MAN!, why didn't Pontiac do this???  It would have been an incredible rivalry.  The feel inside the 88 Porsche is very similar to the 88GT Turbo.  DAMN GM!!!  One mid-engine, one rear-engine, manual steering, 200hp., 2 seaters (useable anyway), sloping front hood,.... I think it would have been awesome to watch the progression of the Fiero into the 21st century.  They could have taken on Porsche, for less than $20K!But alas we shall never know. Oh well.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>Later,<BR>Dave</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">      <BR>Ben Cannon